        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Donchian\n- Organizations: System of a Down\n- Products: Donchian channel\n- Works: The Metro\n- Topics: Armenian-American identity, heavy metal, market trading, managed futures\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Donchian was born in September 1905 in Hartford, Connecticut.\n- Richard Donchian was an Armenian-American commodities and futures trader and a pioneer in managed futures.\n- System of a Down is an Armenian-American heavy metal band from Glendale, California, formed in 1994.\n- Richard Donchian died in 1993.\n- The Donchian channel is a market trading indicator developed by Richard Donchian.\n- The song \"The Metro\" has been covered by System of a Down, Alkaline Trio, John Frusciante, Hannah Fury, Idle Warship, and The Interrupters.",
